  message: "CLOSED done, 2026-09-25 (P2 review, dev e4a47383ab). DONE-AND-NEVER-CLOSED: fixed by d1116cc1af (2026-08-04, \"fix(taint): one right-anchored parser for the symbol-id path slot\"), the day after filing.\n\nTHE ROW'S OWN REPRO, re-run verbatim on dev:\n    from hypergumbo_core.ir import _extract_path_slot\n    _extract_path_slot(\"dart:dart:io:0-0:module:module\")  ->  'dart:io'   (was 'dart')\n\nWHY IT HOLDS, from the code rather than one value:\n- ir._extract_path_slot (ir.py:1793) no longer splits. It delegates to the new chokepoint `ir.symbol_path_slot` (ir.py:1639), which is right-anchored and span-anchored (INV-fokik) and returns None only for a malformed id.\n- The consumer the row named, apply_external_id_remap's referring-site provenance (ir.py:2147 `orig_src_path = _extract_path_slot(edge.src)`), therefore records `dart:io`, not `dart`.\n- `symbol_path_slot(\"dart:dart:io:0-0:module:module\")` also returns 'dart:io'.\n\nNOT ASSERTED: the row's NOT-MEASURED note on corpus blast radius is still unmeasured (no count of colon-bearing path slots was taken). The fix is a total function over the grammar, so that count no longer gates correctness.\n\nThe general \"six homes\" consolidation is WI-ribuz, still open. Its current state is recorded there."  # 8542
